---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<section id="macro">
  <div class="wide-container">
    <div class="section-label">Macro</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Thesis Scoreboard</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Browser refresh checks six public feeds and repeats every 15 minutes while this page is visible; a manual refresh also tries the EIA Brent feed, which uses a shared rate-limited demo endpoint. Spot prices are indicative, and official daily series follow publisher release times. OAT–Bund and DXY remain dated published readings because their current sources block direct browser refresh. Signals and policy triggers are dated evidence snapshots, not a live news scan; unknown means unverified.
    </p>

    <div class="scoreboard-toolbar">
      <button id="scoreboard-refresh" class="refresh-button" type="button">Refresh latest data</button>
      <p id="scoreboard-status" class="scoreboard-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Connecting to public data feeds and loading dated evidence…</p>
    </div>

    <div class="metric-grid" id="macro-metrics" aria-label="Market and macro readings">
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>US total debt</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-debt">$40.07T</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-debt">Baseline · 28 Sep 2026</p><a class="source-link" id="source-debt" href="https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/debt-to-the-penny/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>10Y Treasury yield</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-us10y">~4.95%</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-us10y">Baseline · 28 Sep 2026</p><a class="source-link" id="source-us10y" href="https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>OAT–Bund spread</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-oat">105bp</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-oat">Baseline · 28 Sep 2026</p><a class="source-link" id="source-oat" href="https://www.ideal-investisseur.fr/en/markets/oat-bund-spread.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>Gold</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-gold">~$4,350</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-gold">Baseline · 28 Sep 2026</p><a class="source-link" id="source-gold" href="https://api.gold-api.com/price/XAU" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>Silver</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-silver">+52% YoY</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-silver">Baseline was year-over-year; live feed reports spot price.</p><a class="source-link" id="source-silver" href="https://api.gold-api.com/price/XAG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>Bitcoin</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-btc">$77K</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-btc">Baseline · 28 Sep 2026</p><a class="source-link" id="source-btc" href="https://api.coinbase.com/v2/prices/BTC-USD/spot" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>USD-pegged stablecoins</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-stable">$308B</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-stable">Baseline · 28 Sep 2026</p><a class="source-link" id="source-stable" href="https://stablecoins.llama.fi/stablecoins?includePrices=false" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>Brent crude</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-brent">~$90</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-brent">Baseline · 28 Sep 2026</p><a class="source-link" id="source-brent" href="https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/pet_pri_spt_s1_d.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
      <article class="metric-card"><h3>DXY futures proxy</h3><p class="metric-value" id="metric-dxy">~99.7</p><p class="metric-meta" id="metric-meta-dxy">Baseline · 28 Sep 2026</p><a class="source-link" id="source-dxy" href="https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DX-Y.NYB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a></article>
    </div>

    <p class="data-caveat">
      Baseline values above are the supplied 28 Sep 2026 snapshot, not current quotes. Silver's baseline is a year-over-year change; refreshed silver is a spot quote. A failed or unavailable source leaves its last verified reading in place and marks it stale.
    </p>

    <h3 class="subsection-title">Thesis ratings · supplied snapshot</h3>
    <p class="section-desc compact-desc">These eight entries and their status/strength values come from the supplied 28 Sep 2026 code excerpt. Strength is not a probability. The excerpt is incomplete, so omitted theses are not inferred; refreshed market data does not rewrite these baseline judgments.</p>
    <div class="thesis-grid" aria-label="Baseline thesis ratings">
      <article class="thesis-card"><h4>Long sovereign paper = designated loser</h4><span class="thesis-status winning">WINNING · snapshot</span><strong>95 / 100</strong></article>
      <article class="thesis-card"><h4>Hard-asset rotation</h4><span class="thesis-status winning">WINNING · snapshot</span><strong>90 / 100</strong></article>
      <article class="thesis-card"><h4>Stablecoin → T-bill channel</h4><span class="thesis-status winning">WINNING · snapshot</span><strong>92 / 100</strong></article>
      <article class="thesis-card"><h4>Europe capital exodus</h4><span class="thesis-status winning">WINNING · snapshot</span><strong>85 / 100</strong></article>
      <article class="thesis-card"><h4>Weaponization → fragmentation</h4><span class="thesis-status winning">WINNING · snapshot</span><strong>82 / 100</strong></article>
      <article class="thesis-card"><h4>US capital-friction rising</h4><span class="thesis-status winning">WINNING · snapshot</span><strong>60 / 100</strong></article>
      <article class="thesis-card"><h4>Milkshake vs. de-dollarization</h4><span class="thesis-status contested">CONTESTED · snapshot</span><strong>55 / 100</strong></article>
      <article class="thesis-card"><h4>AI pop vs. AGI buildout</h4><span class="thesis-status contested">CONTESTED · snapshot</span><strong>50 / 100</strong></article>
    </div>

    <h3 class="subsection-title">Rule status</h3>
    <p class="section-desc compact-desc">A rule is marked fired only when its required input is verified. Missing evidence is shown as unknown, never as false. The gold/dollar trend uses COMEX gold and ICE dollar-index continuous-contract closes as proxies; it is not a spot-index calculation.</p>
    <div class="signal-grid" id="signal-grid">
      <article class="signal-card"><h4>OAT–Bund &gt; 90bp</h4><p id="rule-oat90" class="signal-state">Baseline: fired at 105bp · 28 Sep 2026</p></article>
      <article class="signal-card"><h4>OAT–Bund &gt; 130bp</h4><p id="rule-oat130" class="signal-state">Baseline: not fired at 105bp · 28 Sep 2026</p></article>
      <article class="signal-card"><h4>Gold + dollar together</h4><p id="rule-golddxy" class="signal-state">Baseline: not sustained · 28 Sep 2026</p><p class="signal-method">Refresh rule: both daily futures proxies must close above their aligned values from 10 sessions earlier for 3 consecutive closes.</p></article>
      <article class="signal-card"><h4>G7 auction failure</h4><p id="rule-auction" class="signal-state">Unknown · not verified by the supplied excerpt</p></article>
      <article class="signal-card"><h4>Official de-dollarization</h4><p id="rule-dedollar" class="signal-state">Unknown · not verified by the supplied excerpt</p></article>
      <article class="signal-card"><h4>Recapitalization-policy advance</h4><p id="rule-recap" class="signal-state">Unknown · not verified by the supplied excerpt</p></article>
    </div>

    <div class="weight-note" id="weight-note">
      <strong>Scenario weights are not being changed.</strong> The supplied code excerpt names the rules but does not include starting weights or the registered shift sizes. This board will not invent a scoring formula.
    </div>

    <h3 class="subsection-title">Policy trigger states</h3>
    <p class="section-desc compact-desc">States stay unverified until a current source is checked.</p>
    <div class="trigger-grid" id="trigger-grid">
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>GENIUS final rules</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>GENIUS effective</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>Issuer approvals</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>Bitcoin reserve</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>BTC budget-neutral</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>CLARITY Act</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>H.R. 8957</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>Gold revaluation</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
      <div class="trigger-card"><span>Hard-asset backing</span><strong>Unverified</strong></div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="subsection-title">Notable events</h3>
    <p class="section-desc compact-desc" id="macro-events">No verified event feed is connected. No headlines or policy developments are being inferred.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<script is:inline src={`${base}js/scoreboard.js`} defer></script>
